From 5c1467982d743175b3324e61e8c5c5922a00fd86 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 18:50:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(dsv41): cache SP local routing masks and skip SP tail
 pad rows in partials router

Base: 1107 vLLM patch head 320021e3c4dbb202d911ab70e2cd924c75420488.

Rationale:
During sequence-parallel prefill on the 20 encoder layers (0..19), mhc.post_pre casts each rank's L = ceil(T / TP) shard to MXFP8 while sp_moe_inputs calls router.route_local(x, sp_rows, input_ids=input_ids) before sp_rows.gather_mxfp8(x_q, weights, ids):
1. While _routing_masks cached the full T-row image and routed masks on ForwardContext, _local_mask(mask, rows, sp_rows) called sp_rows.local_slice(mask[:sp_rows.num_tokens]) uncached on every encoder layer. Whenever T % TP != 0 (every power-of-2 chunk size T = 256..16384 on TP=3, and any non-multiple of TP on TP=4), the tail rank (rank = TP - 1, where real_rows < local_rows) allocated a new boolean tensor and copied [:real_rows] twice per layer (4 GPU kernel launches per layer, 80 across the 20 encoder layers), adding 8.7-20.5 us/layer (+3% to +44% local router latency) on the tail rank immediately before the synchronous gather_mxfp8 collective. When ForwardContext was not active, _routing_masks also omitted caching _ds41_image_token_mask on sp_rows.
2. In _partials_mask (used by TileLangGateRouter when local_rows <= 256, i.e., 205 <= T <= 768 on TP=3 and 205 <= T <= 1024 on TP=4), _local_mask(is_padding, rows, sp_rows) zero-padded [real_rows:local_rows] with False (active / route) instead of True (padding / skip), causing route_partials to route unused SP tail pad rows as active tokens (and fail T.device_assert(finite) if tail pad rows contained NaN/Inf) instead of skipping them with topk_idx = -1, topk_weights = 0.0 as TileKernelsRouter does when local_rows > 256.

Cache _local_mask slices per step on ForwardContext (or sp_rows when ForwardContext is absent) keyed by (id(mask), num_tokens, world_size, rank, rows, pad) with mask._version validation, cache _ds41_image_token_mask on sp_rows when ForwardContext is absent, and pass pad=True in _partials_mask so SP tail pad rows [real_rows:local_rows] are padded with True (skipped).

Quality:
Bit-identical (torch.equal) on all real rows [0:real_rows] across all ranks and chunk sizes; skips unused SP tail pad rows [real_rows:local_rows] with topk_idx = -1 and topk_weights = 0.0 in route_partials (matching TileKernelsRouter).

Tests:
- pytest --noconftest tests/models/test_deepseek_v4_1_sp_prefill.py tests/kernels/moe/test_deepseek_v41_tilelang_router.py (262 passed across 2 fresh container boots).

Upstream status: local SP prefill router optimization and tail-padding fix for DeepSeek V4.1 TileLang router.
